--!native
--!strict
--[[
	================================================================================
	DIAGNOSTICS CORE  ::  DiagnosticsCore.luau
	================================================================================
	Advanced Client-Side Diagnostic & Network Telemetry Instrumentation Engine

	Classification : Authorized Internal QA Performance Profiling & Network
	                 Diagnostic Tool
	Target         : Standard Roblox Runtime (Client-Server), Luau 5.1+
	Directives     : --!strict, --!native

	--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
	OPERATIONAL PROFILE
	--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
	This build is deliberately VERBOSE. Every intercepted packet, attribute
	mutation, route event and subsystem transition emits a structured audit line to
	the developer console the moment it occurs. It is the inverse policy of a silent
	release build and must not be shipped to production clients without a console
	budget review.

	LAYER A : Global Network Interceptor & Packet Logger
	          Traverses configured roots (ReplicatedStorage, ReplicatedFirst,
	          Workspace, LocalPlayer), wraps FireServer / InvokeServer on every
	          RemoteEvent, UnreliableRemoteEvent and RemoteFunction found, keeps
	          watching for late-created remotes via DescendantAdded, and attaches
	          observation listeners for inbound OnClientEvent / OnClientInvoke.

	LAYER B : Local Player Attribute & State Surveillance
	          Real-time attribute tracking with a priority watchlist (BanReason,
	          session flags, team assignments), automatic discovery of new
	          attributes, and immediate console notification on every mutation.

	LAYER C : Session & Route Telemetry Monitor
	          Environment initialisation (game.Loaded), route metadata
	          (PlaceId / GameId / JobId / PlaceVersion / IsStudio), character
	          session transitions, and TeleportService routing captures.

	LAYER D : Self-Contained Execution
	          ASCII boot banner and a protective boot block at the bottom of the
	          file. Every hook in every layer is pcall-isolated.

	--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
	IMPLEMENTATION NOTES THE SPEC DID NOT COVER
	--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
	1. COLOR OUTPUT
	   Roblox's Studio output pane does not interpret ANSI escape sequences, and
	   print() has no rich-text mode. Emitting raw escape codes there prints literal
	   control characters. This engine therefore colour-codes by CHANNEL:

	     print() -> debug / info / net / attr / route / metric   (white)
	     warn()  -> warn / error levels                           (amber in Studio)

	   An ANSI palette is included and can be enabled with
	   Console.SetANSI(true) when logs are piped to a terminal
	   (RunInRoblox / Lune / CI capture), where escape codes DO render.

	2. PAYLOAD REDACTION
	   A tool that prints every payload will print credentials if the game sends
	   any. Keys matching Config.redact.keys are replaced with "<redacted>" before
	   serialisation, at any depth. This is on by default.

	3. OBSERVATION LIMITS (stated, not silently skipped)
	   Wrapping an instance member covers every caller in THIS client VM. It does
	   not observe other VMs, and it cannot intercept calls a script made before
	   tracking began. Inbound traffic is observed through listeners this engine
	   connects itself; it cannot see listeners other scripts registered.
	   Remote members are locked on some clients; a rejected wrap is reported in the
	   console as [WRAP-DENIED] and counting continues at the call-site API instead.

	4. VOLUME GOVERNANCE
	   Verbose logging is bounded by Config.console.rateLimitPerSecond (default 120)
	   and Config.console.payloadPreviewChars (default 220). When the budget is
	   exhausted the engine prints a single [THROTTLED] notice with the suppressed
	   count and keeps recording into the ring buffer, so the audit trail stays
	   complete even when the console display is throttled.
	================================================================================
]]

